WEBVTT

00:01.174 --> 00:04.551
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.606 --> 00:07.933
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.984 --> 00:11.412
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.581 --> 00:14.490
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.747 --> 00:18.293
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.344 --> 00:21.503
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.572 --> 00:23.109
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.160 --> 00:24.532
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.616 --> 00:27.218
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.450 --> 00:35.503
All right, ladies,

00:35.571 --> 00:37.327
let's pick teams
for dodgeball.

00:37.394 --> 00:38.331
Connie, would you like
to be a captain?

00:38.398 --> 00:39.434
Sure.

00:39.502 --> 00:41.441
I pick everyone
except Meg.

00:41.509 --> 00:43.147
Fair enough. Go!
(blows whistle)

00:43.215 --> 00:45.739
(yelling)

00:45.824 --> 00:47.930
Oww!

00:47.999 --> 00:50.089
(whirring)

00:55.560 --> 00:57.933
(bell rings)

00:58.000 --> 00:59.773
Hey, where's
everybody going?

00:59.840 --> 01:01.780
That's not how we end
this class.

01:03.431 --> 01:04.497
Good job today.
(kisses)

01:04.522 --> 01:05.734
Good job today.
(kisses)

01:05.759 --> 01:07.063
Great class.
(kisses)

01:07.088 --> 01:08.151
Nice hustle.
(kisses)

01:11.934 --> 01:13.324
Hey, how was gym class?

01:13.325 --> 01:14.117
Terrible.

01:14.118 --> 01:15.153
You know, I don't think
I can take

01:15.222 --> 01:16.207
another semester
at this school, Ruth.

01:16.275 --> 01:17.712
It's torture.

01:17.780 --> 01:20.489
It's worse than sitting
next to a baby on an airplane.

01:21.895 --> 01:23.366
So what brings you
to Kentucky?

01:23.433 --> 01:24.603
I'm visiting my family.

01:24.671 --> 01:26.243
Ah, family man.

01:26.311 --> 01:28.718
Me? Single
and ready to mingle.

01:28.786 --> 01:31.595
Tom Brunell's the name.
Insurance is the game.

01:31.663 --> 01:35.375
<i>And right now,
the game is very good to me.</i>

01:35.443 --> 01:36.595
Hey, I know!

01:36.664 --> 01:37.699
If you hate it
so much here,

01:37.767 --> 01:38.804
why don't you
come to Paris

01:38.872 --> 01:40.192
for a semester
with me instead?

01:40.260 --> 01:41.380
I'm leaving next week.

01:41.447 --> 01:43.185
You're going to Paris
for a semester?

01:43.253 --> 01:45.260
Yeah, it's a program
sponsored by the high school.

01:45.328 --> 01:46.932
My aunt even has
an apartment there

01:47.000 --> 01:48.438
that we can stay in
for free.

01:48.506 --> 01:50.913
Oh, my God,
that sounds so amazing!

01:50.981 --> 01:52.435
Excuse me,
I was wondering

01:52.503 --> 01:55.011
if you would go to the dance
with me on Friday.

01:55.096 --> 01:56.566
Chris, it's me, Meg.

01:56.634 --> 01:57.402
(sighing)

01:57.470 --> 01:58.607
Well, that's everybody.

02:03.224 --> 02:06.367
<i>TV ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Ethiopian Hoarders.</i>

02:06.436 --> 02:09.579
(sobbing): I don't know
how it got like this!

02:09.646 --> 02:11.152
Dad, Mom,

02:11.220 --> 02:12.590
there's something
I want to ask you.

02:12.657 --> 02:13.827
Can I go to school
in Paris

02:13.895 --> 02:14.831
for a semester?

02:14.899 --> 02:16.269
What? Paris?

02:16.337 --> 02:18.076
Hey, you know,
I have a pen pal in Paris.

02:18.144 --> 02:19.531
Would you mind bringing him
this letter?

02:19.599 --> 02:21.487
(hocking phlegm)

02:21.556 --> 02:22.844
We're fighting.

02:22.911 --> 02:25.369
Meg, I'd love to send you
to Paris for a semester,

02:25.436 --> 02:26.790
but we can't afford that.

02:26.874 --> 02:28.061
But I can pay
for it myself.

02:28.129 --> 02:29.834
I've been saving up
from all my part-time jobs.

02:29.903 --> 02:31.240
That's smart of you, Meg.

02:31.307 --> 02:32.444
You know, sometimes I do

02:32.512 --> 02:34.618
part-time jobs
for extra cash.

02:36.124 --> 02:37.645
Gimme money. Gimme money.
(violin screeching)

02:37.696 --> 02:39.701
Gimme money. Gimme money.
Gimme money.

02:46.277 --> 02:47.780
You be careful,
sweetie,

02:47.848 --> 02:49.487
and call us as soon
as the plane lands.

02:49.538 --> 02:50.841
Okay, Mom, I will.

02:50.910 --> 02:52.247
I'll miss you, Dad.

02:52.315 --> 02:54.422
I've never been very good
at saying good-bee.

02:54.506 --> 02:56.211
Good-bee, Meg.

02:56.279 --> 02:57.548
And I'm gonna
bring you back

02:57.617 --> 02:59.339
something special,
little guy.

02:59.406 --> 03:01.647
Don't worry about me.
Just get yourself laid.

03:01.715 --> 03:03.955
Will you get me
French Stewart's autograph?

03:04.023 --> 03:05.594
Say hello
to the Pont Neuf for me,

03:05.662 --> 03:07.836
or as I like to call it,
my inspiration point...

03:07.903 --> 03:08.905
Oh, you're gone.

03:08.974 --> 03:10.311
And the family's gone.

03:16.216 --> 03:17.787
(tires screeching)

03:17.855 --> 03:20.347
Oh, my God, we're
actually here in Paris.

03:20.431 --> 03:22.872
This is so exciting!

03:22.940 --> 03:24.343
(French accent):
Good day, foreigners.

03:24.411 --> 03:27.321
On behalf of the country
of France, we surrender.

03:27.390 --> 03:29.629
Oh, my God,
I love your breath.

03:29.697 --> 03:30.733
Hi, I'm Meg.

03:30.801 --> 03:33.158
This is my friend, Ruth.

03:33.226 --> 03:35.142
Would you ladies
like to share a cab,

03:35.210 --> 03:37.935
Or as we say,
"sharre a cabbuh"?

03:38.003 --> 03:38.939
Sure.

03:39.007 --> 03:40.210
That sounds great.

03:40.278 --> 03:42.150
Oh, and please
do not be suspicious

03:42.218 --> 03:43.655
that I am
at the airport

03:43.722 --> 03:45.463
with no baggage
whatsoever.

03:47.419 --> 03:50.546
A cool name to say
with a French accent

03:50.614 --> 03:52.520
is Ashtahn Kootchere.

03:55.749 --> 03:56.517
Bye!

03:56.585 --> 03:57.571
Thanks!

04:01.001 --> 04:02.238
Hey, it's me.

04:02.306 --> 04:03.978
I've got
some fresh arrivals for you.

04:04.046 --> 04:05.650
How are they?

04:05.718 --> 04:07.223
<i>On a scale from un to dix,</i>

04:07.290 --> 04:10.132
<i>they're about a trois.</i>

04:11.422 --> 04:13.294
Wow, this place
is awesome!

04:13.361 --> 04:14.665
I know!

04:14.732 --> 04:16.773
Hey, you wanna dance around
like morons to loud music?

04:16.840 --> 04:17.944
(rock music playing)

04:17.995 --> 04:19.314
I'll be right back.

04:19.366 --> 04:21.640
I've been holding in
a dump since America.

04:24.986 --> 04:26.256
(phone ringing)

04:26.324 --> 04:28.079
Griffin residence.

04:28.146 --> 04:29.350
Hi, Dad, it's me.

04:29.402 --> 04:31.324
Just wanted you to know
I got here safe.

04:31.392 --> 04:32.094
(alarmed):
And sound?

04:32.161 --> 04:34.101
Yes, Dad, and sound.

04:34.168 --> 04:35.238
(relieved):
Oh, good.

04:35.306 --> 04:37.295
The "sound" is what concerns me.

04:37.363 --> 04:39.202
Oh, it's so amazing here, Dad.
Yep.

04:39.270 --> 04:40.808
You should see it.
Uh-huh.

04:40.875 --> 04:42.413
The apartment we're staying in is huge,
Uh-huh.

04:42.482 --> 04:43.785
and has an incredible view of...
Uh-huh.

04:43.853 --> 04:44.855
(gasping)

04:44.923 --> 04:46.126
Dad, something's
going on.

04:46.194 --> 04:47.330
Some men just broke in.

04:50.142 --> 04:51.780
(gasps) Oh, my God!
They've got Ruth!

04:51.848 --> 04:53.184
(footsteps approaching)

04:53.252 --> 04:55.610
And now, I think
they're coming after me!

04:55.678 --> 04:56.848
(serious):
All right, Meg,

04:56.916 --> 04:58.955
I need you to listen to me
very carefully:

04:59.023 --> 05:00.058
panic.

05:00.128 --> 05:01.498
Pay no attention to detail.

05:01.566 --> 05:03.270
Let your mind race.

05:03.338 --> 05:05.076
Take short, rapid breaths.

05:05.145 --> 05:06.750
Then hide under the bed,

05:06.818 --> 05:08.656
but leave two of your feet
sticking out.

05:10.598 --> 05:12.101
(footsteps approaching)

05:15.080 --> 05:16.099
(whispering):
Oh, my God, Dad!

05:16.167 --> 05:18.123
Are they gonna take me?
I'm so scared!

05:18.191 --> 05:19.495
(screaming)

05:19.563 --> 05:21.033
Meg? Meg?

05:21.102 --> 05:25.616
(man breathing heavily)

05:25.685 --> 05:28.727
I don't know who you are.
I don't know what you want.

05:28.778 --> 05:31.738
But I have a very particular
lack of skills.

05:31.789 --> 05:34.130
I will never be able
to find you,

05:34.215 --> 05:36.086
but what I do have
is two dollars

05:36.137 --> 05:37.692
and a Casio wristwatch.

05:37.759 --> 05:39.583
You can have one of them.

05:39.651 --> 05:41.990
(deep, menacing voice):
Drakkar Noir.

05:42.059 --> 05:43.362
(hangs up)

05:43.430 --> 05:44.834
These guys are serious.

05:44.902 --> 05:46.574
Lois, Meg's dead!

05:49.886 --> 05:52.461
Please, there's gotta be
something you can do!

05:52.530 --> 05:54.736
My little girl is
in terrible danger!

05:54.804 --> 05:56.274
Ma'am, the men
who took your daughter

05:56.343 --> 05:57.546
are most likely members

05:57.615 --> 05:59.519
of a sophisticated network
of human smugglers.

05:59.587 --> 06:01.493
If she's not found
within 96 hours,

06:01.561 --> 06:03.701
chances are
she's gone forever.

06:03.769 --> 06:05.140
Then we've gotta hurry!

06:05.208 --> 06:06.678
Sorry, we can't
begin our search

06:06.746 --> 06:08.886
until she's been missing
for 96 hours.

06:08.954 --> 06:11.061
Oh, my God! My baby!

06:11.129 --> 06:13.135
Yeah, there's a pretty grisly
sex trade over there.

06:13.202 --> 06:15.978
Usually we just end up
burying framed pictures.

06:16.047 --> 06:17.918
Oh, Peter!
This is a nightmare!

06:17.986 --> 06:19.892
(sobbing)

06:21.715 --> 06:23.136
What's going on
down there?

06:23.205 --> 06:24.174
Are they gonna
find her?

06:24.241 --> 06:25.311
Doesn't look good.

06:25.379 --> 06:27.250
Stewie, I think
there's only one way

06:27.318 --> 06:28.890
we're ever gonna
see Meg again.

06:28.958 --> 06:31.064
You and I have to take matters
into our own hands.

06:31.133 --> 06:32.670
What? What are you
talking about?

06:32.738 --> 06:34.292
Look, you're the only one
who's got the know-how

06:34.360 --> 06:36.283
and the technology
to help us track her down.

06:36.351 --> 06:37.804
Hmm. Interesting.

06:37.857 --> 06:39.828
Last week, all my gadgets
were "hooey,"

06:39.913 --> 06:41.117
I think was the word.

06:41.168 --> 06:43.107
I didn't say...
You said "hooey"!

06:43.175 --> 06:44.345
All right, I've booked us
on a flight

06:44.412 --> 06:45.950
that leaves in two hours,

06:46.018 --> 06:48.493
so, um, whose credit card
shall we put it on?

06:48.561 --> 06:50.132
Just put it on yours
and I'll pay you back.

06:50.200 --> 06:51.637
Yeah, I feel like
when that happens,

06:51.705 --> 06:53.009
I sometimes don't
get paid back.

06:53.076 --> 06:54.481
Like when?

06:54.549 --> 06:56.823
<i>Jersey Boys, Morton's
Steakhouse, Foxwoods...</i>

06:56.890 --> 06:58.930
<i>Foxwoods and Jersey Boys
was the same trip!</i>

06:58.997 --> 07:00.435
(sighing):
You know what? Fine.

07:00.521 --> 07:02.091
I'll-I'll put it
on my card,

07:02.160 --> 07:03.730
but I-I-I'm just gonna say
it's a gift

07:03.797 --> 07:05.637
because that's the only way
I can do this anymore.

07:10.720 --> 07:12.593
All right, the first thing
we've got to do when we land

07:12.661 --> 07:14.450
is check the apartment
where Meg was abducted

07:14.517 --> 07:15.787
and see if we can find
some clues.

07:15.855 --> 07:17.526
That sounds good.
That's what I was thinking.

07:17.594 --> 07:19.701
Excuse me, do you mind
if we switch seats

07:19.769 --> 07:21.708
so my family can sit
all together?

07:21.776 --> 07:23.715
No, we don't...
we-we don't switch.

07:23.783 --> 07:25.054
'Cause when we booked,

07:25.121 --> 07:26.626
they didn't have
three together...

07:26.694 --> 07:28.298
Ma'am, ma'am,
your poor planning

07:28.366 --> 07:30.305
does not constitute
an emergency for me.

07:30.373 --> 07:33.015
You'll see him in Paris.
Go sit down.

07:33.083 --> 07:35.657
God, Meg's kidnappers could be
anywhere in France by now.

07:35.726 --> 07:37.565
Well, we do have
one lead, Brian.

07:37.633 --> 07:39.639
I have a recording
of the kidnapper's voice.

07:39.706 --> 07:41.428
What? You do? How?

07:41.479 --> 07:42.782
I recorded
the kidnapper's phone call

07:42.850 --> 07:43.987
with the fat man.

07:44.055 --> 07:45.358
You see, Brian,
I record

07:45.427 --> 07:47.733
all phone calls coming in
or out of the house.

07:47.801 --> 07:49.272
Y-Y-You do?

07:49.340 --> 07:51.647
Yep. This one's
one of my faves.

07:51.716 --> 07:54.858
WOMAN: Hello, Fundamental Industries.
How can I help you?

07:54.926 --> 07:56.532
BRIAN: Yeah, um, is this...
is this Bang Brothers?

07:56.600 --> 07:58.271
WOMAN:
Yes.

07:58.339 --> 08:00.713
BRIAN: Oh. Okay. I-I-I'd like
to cancel my subscription.

08:00.780 --> 08:01.850
WOMAN:
Uh, what's your name?

08:01.918 --> 08:03.189
BRIAN:
Brian Griffin.

08:03.256 --> 08:04.593
WOMAN: And which site
did you belong to?

08:04.661 --> 08:07.102
BRIAN:
Uh... Captain Stabbin'.

08:07.169 --> 08:08.741
WOMAN:
And how are you spelling that?

08:08.808 --> 08:11.050
BRIAN:
Uh... uh, "Captain", full word,

08:11.118 --> 08:14.160
then "Stabbin',"
S-T-A-B-B-I-N apostrophe.

08:14.228 --> 08:17.807
WOMAN:
Okay, I'm checking.

08:17.875 --> 08:21.419
BRIAN: You know, in-instead
of a "G" at the end.

08:21.488 --> 08:22.892
WOMAN: I'm sorry, sir.
I'm not finding that site.

08:22.959 --> 08:24.832
Uh, what was the subject matter?

08:24.900 --> 08:27.507
BRIAN: Um... a guy
doing chicks on a boat

08:27.575 --> 08:29.247
in a, uh, captain's hat.

08:29.315 --> 08:31.321
WOMAN:
Okay, I'm checking.

08:31.389 --> 08:33.195
BRIAN: The, um...
(clearing throat)

08:33.262 --> 08:34.935
the, passengers had, uh,
just signed up

08:35.002 --> 08:36.539
for a tour of the harbor

08:36.608 --> 08:38.613
and then
all that stuff happened.

08:38.682 --> 08:40.085
Okay, you made
your point.

08:44.820 --> 08:46.291
(tires screeching)

08:48.282 --> 08:49.853
Well, this is where
Meg was staying.

08:49.921 --> 08:52.060
Oh. I thought Paris would be
a bit more picturesque.

08:52.129 --> 08:53.367
Instead it's just traffic

08:53.434 --> 08:55.841
and some big guy
using a jackhammer.

08:55.910 --> 08:58.082
But monsieur,
ziss is not a jackhammer.

08:58.150 --> 09:00.090
It is a "Jacqueshammer."

09:00.158 --> 09:03.435
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-
ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-

09:03.520 --> 09:05.710
ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-
ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho...

09:08.153 --> 09:09.974
Oh, God, it's worse
than I imagined.

09:10.042 --> 09:11.262
You know, maybe
it'd help

09:11.330 --> 09:13.237
if we just tried
to track Meg's movements

09:13.304 --> 09:14.558
from the moment
she arrived in France.

09:14.625 --> 09:15.778
That's a good idea, Brian.

09:15.846 --> 09:17.200
Let's try Google Earth.

09:17.268 --> 09:18.205
Worth a shot.

09:20.614 --> 09:22.084
There. Enhance.

09:28.892 --> 09:30.732
Wow, I never knew you could
do this on a computer.

09:30.800 --> 09:32.773
'Course not, you spend
all your time on this

09:32.840 --> 09:34.344
watching Captain Stabbin'.

09:34.412 --> 09:36.318
All right, we've got
to find this man.

09:36.385 --> 09:38.592
Let's see, this was
taken at the airport.

09:38.661 --> 09:40.031
He could be
some sort of lookout

09:40.099 --> 09:41.837
who spots girls
fresh off the plane.

09:41.905 --> 09:44.012
Yes, you're probably right,
Brian. Such scum.

09:44.080 --> 09:45.718
I'll bet they target
young girls

09:45.786 --> 09:48.093
the way Army commercials
target minorities.

09:48.160 --> 09:49.314
Hey.

09:49.381 --> 09:50.853
Other black guys.

09:50.921 --> 09:52.375
It ain't so bad.

10:00.002 --> 10:01.925
Oh, my God, Stewie!
There he is!

10:01.976 --> 10:03.648
Hey, buddy, we've got
a few questions for you!

10:03.733 --> 10:07.528
Excuse me, but this is
a "smoking only" area.

10:07.596 --> 10:09.168
Oh, sorry.
Do you have a, uh...

10:11.777 --> 10:15.173
You know, I really only smoke
when I drink.

10:15.224 --> 10:17.597
Oh. Well, this is nice.

10:17.666 --> 10:19.737
This is a nice way
to do this.

10:19.806 --> 10:22.315
Look, we need to know:
have you seen this girl?

10:23.887 --> 10:25.525
Quick!
He's getting away!

10:28.688 --> 10:30.493
Oh, no, he's one of those
parkour, free-running guys.

10:30.560 --> 10:32.215
We'll never catch him!

10:36.315 --> 10:37.651
(horn blaring)

10:37.719 --> 10:39.090
(gasping)

10:39.158 --> 10:42.368
(weakly): Oh, no. I have
chateau'ed myself.

10:42.437 --> 10:44.242
(groaning)

10:44.309 --> 10:46.751
Damn it. He died before he could
tell us anything.

10:46.819 --> 10:47.787
Brian, he's
the first guy.

10:47.855 --> 10:49.460
The first guy
always dies.

10:49.528 --> 10:51.015
Well, I'm sure
he didn't work alone.

10:51.100 --> 10:52.639
Maybe there's something
in here we can use.

10:52.706 --> 10:54.862
(Velcro ripping) Ugh, this guy has
a Velcro wallet.

10:54.930 --> 10:55.900
Grow up.

10:59.715 --> 11:02.071
All right, this is the address
that was in his wallet.

11:02.140 --> 11:03.460
Yeah, but how are we
gonna know for sure

11:03.527 --> 11:04.847
if these are the guys
who took Meg?

11:04.898 --> 11:07.507
Well, we have the kidnapper's
voice on tape, remember?

11:07.575 --> 11:09.229
(deep, menacing voice):
Drakkar Noir.

11:09.298 --> 11:11.270
I can use the voice
recognition software

11:11.338 --> 11:13.044
in this recorder
to confirm a match.

11:13.112 --> 11:14.031
Now, here.

11:14.098 --> 11:15.368
Take this briefcase.

11:16.674 --> 11:18.196
We're Eastern European
cologne salesmen.

11:18.263 --> 11:19.567
We ask them
what they want,

11:19.635 --> 11:21.206
and when they say
"Drakkar Noir"--

11:21.273 --> 11:22.310
which they all will--

11:22.378 --> 11:24.017
we'll know
if we have our man.

11:25.305 --> 11:26.542
MAN:
Drakkar Noir?

11:27.747 --> 11:28.816
(buzzer sounding)

11:28.883 --> 11:29.953
All right, well,
that's not him,

11:30.021 --> 11:31.493
but this is
gonna be easy.

11:34.437 --> 11:36.074
Well, gentlemen,
now that you have smelled

11:36.143 --> 11:38.317
all of our colognes,
what'll it be?

11:38.385 --> 11:39.956
I will take
some Drakkar Noir.

11:41.929 --> 11:42.867
How 'bout you?

11:42.934 --> 11:44.238
I am disgusting,

11:44.305 --> 11:46.311
so I will take
two bottle Drakkar Noir.

11:47.583 --> 11:48.820
How 'bout you, chief?

11:48.888 --> 11:50.125
Hmm.

11:50.193 --> 11:52.299
Let me quickly grow beard
and think about it.

11:54.909 --> 11:56.347
I will take
Drakkar Noir.

12:12.020 --> 12:13.474
(both grunting)

12:13.559 --> 12:14.779
What the hell
are you doing?!

12:14.864 --> 12:15.984
We haven't eaten
since the plane.

12:16.068 --> 12:17.037
I'm starving.

12:26.940 --> 12:28.227
Where is this girl?

12:28.295 --> 12:29.565
Where is she?!

12:29.632 --> 12:31.103
We keep girls upstairs.

12:31.171 --> 12:32.809
I hope you burn in hell
along with the guy

12:32.877 --> 12:35.720
who came up with
stuffing a turkey.

12:35.788 --> 12:37.325
Hey!

12:37.393 --> 12:40.102
Who wants to try
some of my "Butthole Bread"?

12:42.160 --> 12:43.195
Meg?

12:43.264 --> 12:44.116
Meg?

12:46.208 --> 12:48.013
Help... me.

12:48.081 --> 12:50.689
Oh, we're here to help
somebody else, sweetheart.

12:50.740 --> 12:51.926
Go, go, go, go. Don't...
Don't look at her.

12:51.994 --> 12:53.281
Don't look at her.
That was my mistake.

12:57.045 --> 12:58.584
Stewie, I don't see
Meg anywhere.

12:58.652 --> 12:59.788
Brian, look!

12:59.856 --> 13:03.468
(sobbing)

13:03.535 --> 13:04.690
Oh, my God!

13:04.757 --> 13:05.709
Meg!

13:05.777 --> 13:06.712
What the hell?

13:06.781 --> 13:07.850
Where'd you get that hat?

13:07.917 --> 13:09.522
Uh, a girl
gave it to me.

13:09.590 --> 13:10.743
Well, what did she
look like?

13:10.811 --> 13:12.818
She had a great
personality.

13:12.885 --> 13:14.055
That's her.

13:14.123 --> 13:15.493
Where is she?
Is she here?

13:15.562 --> 13:18.036
No, uh, they took her
just a little while ago.

13:18.105 --> 13:19.675
Every Wednesday night,

13:19.744 --> 13:21.114
they auction
some of the girls off.

13:21.181 --> 13:22.217
Wednesday?

13:22.285 --> 13:23.287
What a weird night

13:23.355 --> 13:25.027
to auction girls off
into slavery.

13:25.095 --> 13:26.566
Well, you know,
on the weekend,

13:26.634 --> 13:27.536
people probably
have plans.

13:27.604 --> 13:28.774
Have plans?

13:28.841 --> 13:30.012
What are you doing
that's more important

13:30.080 --> 13:31.350
than buying somebody?

13:31.417 --> 13:32.471
Look, where is
this place?

13:32.538 --> 13:33.507
Where do they have
the auction?

13:33.576 --> 13:34.611
I don't know,

13:34.679 --> 13:36.451
but there is
a courtesy shuttle

13:36.520 --> 13:37.890
that runs
every 20 minutes.

13:37.958 --> 13:39.061
What?

13:41.169 --> 13:42.673
Aw, damn it.
We just missed it.

13:42.741 --> 13:44.112
What do you wanna do
for 20 minutes?

13:44.180 --> 13:45.115
Well, I don't know
'bout you,

13:45.183 --> 13:46.253
but I'm gonna work out.

13:46.320 --> 13:47.590
That's how you stay in shape.

13:47.658 --> 13:49.180
You just fit it in
when you have free time,

13:49.248 --> 13:50.451
wherever you are,
wherever you can.

13:50.536 --> 13:52.207
There's semen on this floor.

13:56.623 --> 13:57.458
Stewie, look!

13:59.300 --> 14:00.235
We gotta get in there!

14:01.408 --> 14:02.794
Hey, got one more here!

14:02.862 --> 14:04.099
( Southern falsetto):
Oh, where are we?

14:04.166 --> 14:05.521
I'm from Atlanta.

14:05.589 --> 14:07.360
I don't know
where we are!

14:07.428 --> 14:09.501
Hey, you better hurry.
They're starting soon.

14:10.707 --> 14:11.776
You know what's messed up?

14:11.844 --> 14:13.081
This is all for charity.

14:13.148 --> 14:15.188
All the proceeds
are going to Oxfam.

14:24.605 --> 14:26.277
I hope we're not too late.

14:26.361 --> 14:27.700
You should not
be out here.

14:27.768 --> 14:29.171
Bidding is about to start.
What the hell?

14:29.239 --> 14:31.078
Stewie!

14:33.689 --> 14:35.593
(exotic music playing)

14:35.644 --> 14:39.625
FEMALE AUCTIONEER:
The current bid is $200,000.

14:39.693 --> 14:40.763
Oh, my God.

14:40.830 --> 14:43.405
AUCTIONEER:
Going once, twice...

14:43.472 --> 14:45.546
Sold for $200,000.

14:45.614 --> 14:47.586
Remember:

14:47.654 --> 14:50.311
There is cash back
when you use your Visa Gold.

14:50.364 --> 14:52.956
Our next item appears to be
a late entry.

14:53.007 --> 14:54.494
It is not in the catalog.

14:54.562 --> 14:56.467
BRIAN:
What the hell?

14:56.535 --> 14:58.207
All right, fellas,
bring the lights up a bit,

14:58.275 --> 15:00.816
play the CD I gave you
and let's do this!

15:00.868 --> 15:02.623
("California Gurls"
by Katy Perry playing)

15:02.690 --> 15:04.964
♪ California girls,
we're unforgettable ♪

15:05.033 --> 15:07.423
Ah, that's right.
You like that?

15:07.507 --> 15:09.881
I have $50,000.
♪ Daisy Dukes, bikinis on top ♪

15:09.932 --> 15:11.906
I have $75,000.
♪ Sun-kissed skin so hot ♪

15:11.990 --> 15:13.578
Thank you, Brett Ratner.
♪ We'll melt your popsicle... ♪

15:13.663 --> 15:15.234
Do I have $100,000?

15:15.285 --> 15:17.575
Oh, for God's sake.
$500,000.

15:17.628 --> 15:20.051
We have $500,000.

15:20.102 --> 15:22.058
Going once, going twice,

15:22.109 --> 15:23.698
sold...

15:23.765 --> 15:26.491
to the man
who doesn't quite get auctions.

15:26.559 --> 15:28.297
That was so fun.

15:28.381 --> 15:29.786
How do you
be paying?

15:29.854 --> 15:31.459
Oh, I, uh, I don't
have any money.

15:31.527 --> 15:32.830
Can we work it out,

15:32.898 --> 15:35.137
uh, maybe, some...
other way?

15:35.188 --> 15:36.560
Wait a minute.

15:36.628 --> 15:38.667
Something doesn't
smell funny here.

15:38.752 --> 15:39.938
You're not Arab!

15:40.006 --> 15:42.030
You two are coming
with me.

15:42.097 --> 15:43.702
AUCTIONEER:
This next girl is perfect

15:43.770 --> 15:45.776
for those of you
who want to buy a sex slave

15:45.843 --> 15:48.452
but don't want to spend
sex-slave money.

15:48.520 --> 15:49.656
Oh, my God, Meg!

15:49.724 --> 15:51.763
Wonder what music
they're gonna use for her?

15:51.831 --> 15:56.413
("Let's Make A Deal"
zonk musical cue playing)

15:58.521 --> 15:59.691
Huh, seems about right.

16:06.005 --> 16:08.262
Damn it. We were so close
to saving Meg.

16:08.346 --> 16:09.884
Hey, where's my sister?

16:09.935 --> 16:13.431
She's probably having
her shish kabobbed as we speak.

16:13.499 --> 16:16.040
<i>I heard that from Samantha
in Sex and the City 2.</i>

16:16.108 --> 16:17.912
Ah-ba-ba-ba-ba,
I haven't seen it yet.

16:17.980 --> 16:19.451
That doesn't hurt
the story.

16:19.519 --> 16:21.108
And now prepare to...

16:22.396 --> 16:24.185
We have a jail cell.

16:24.252 --> 16:25.472
I always tell them,

16:25.540 --> 16:27.480
"Put the prisoners
in the jail cell,"

16:27.548 --> 16:30.089
but they always say,
"Just chain 'em up to a pipe."

16:30.157 --> 16:31.343
Idiots.

16:32.549 --> 16:34.254
Hey, that was some
good teamwork, Brian.

16:34.322 --> 16:35.759
We were like Lewis and Clark

16:35.827 --> 16:38.017
and the guy who likes
to tip over canoes.

16:38.084 --> 16:39.991
Ugh, these rapids
are treacherous.

16:40.042 --> 16:41.948
We should reach calmer waters
by nightfall.

16:42.016 --> 16:43.536
Uh-oh!
Earthquake!

16:43.587 --> 16:44.557
Hey, come on!

16:44.641 --> 16:45.846
Careful!

16:47.904 --> 16:49.390
Damn it. Why is he
still with us?

16:49.441 --> 16:50.661
I know!

16:50.729 --> 16:52.168
Until now, walking
to the other end

16:52.235 --> 16:54.342
of the United States seemed
like such a good job.

16:57.152 --> 16:58.055
There she is! Hurry!

17:00.648 --> 17:01.818
Stewie, what are you doing?

17:01.886 --> 17:03.859
We'll never catch
a speeding car on foot.

17:03.927 --> 17:05.465
Haven't you ever seen
an action movie?

17:05.533 --> 17:06.970
All we have to do

17:07.037 --> 17:09.696
is cut diagonally
across any nearby field.

17:13.477 --> 17:14.914
(tires screeching)

17:14.982 --> 17:15.834
See?

17:15.919 --> 17:17.992
(tires screeching)

17:24.466 --> 17:26.756
Aw, crap, they're taking her
onto that yacht.

17:26.825 --> 17:28.796
(engine whirring)

17:32.812 --> 17:34.182
All right, we just gotta
catch up to the boat.

17:34.233 --> 17:35.404
Well, how we
gonna do that?

17:35.472 --> 17:38.314
Oh, cool!
They got Car Chase GPS.

17:39.736 --> 17:42.178
FEMALE GPS VOICE:
Back up dangerously into traffic.

17:42.246 --> 17:44.720
(engine revving)

17:44.771 --> 17:47.011
(tires screeching)

17:47.079 --> 17:51.360
Proceed wrong way
down busy street for 500 meters.

17:51.428 --> 17:52.781
(engine revving)

17:52.833 --> 17:54.923
(horns honking)

17:54.975 --> 17:57.181
(tires screeching)

17:57.265 --> 17:59.906
Say "hang on"
and drive down staircase.

17:59.975 --> 18:01.530
Hang on!

18:01.614 --> 18:03.336
(wheels thumping)

18:05.461 --> 18:06.630
(tires screeching,
horns honking)

18:09.475 --> 18:13.656
Poorly edited shot where driver
is obviously stuntperson.

18:25.181 --> 18:27.321
Leave fart in closed car
like a dick.

18:27.389 --> 18:29.060
BRIAN:
Sorry about that!

18:31.637 --> 18:33.644
All right, they're probably
holding her below deck.

18:33.728 --> 18:35.566
You take the right side.
I'll take the left.

18:35.617 --> 18:36.955
You're gonna need this.

18:37.039 --> 18:38.778
What? I-I-I've never
killed anybody before.

18:38.829 --> 18:39.999
Relax, they're Arabs.

18:40.084 --> 18:42.508
People will still be rooting
for you.

18:42.592 --> 18:43.511
Hey!

18:44.767 --> 18:47.158
Son of a bitch.

18:49.416 --> 18:51.523
Oh. This is like
a video game.

18:54.334 --> 18:56.105
Ah, I'm kinda good at this.

18:58.582 --> 19:00.538
Later, dink.

19:05.289 --> 19:06.559
(gun clicking)

19:10.358 --> 19:11.527
(growling)

19:19.974 --> 19:21.696
(gunshot)

19:24.156 --> 19:25.861
That's for shooting
one of our guys!

19:25.929 --> 19:26.998
(cheering)

19:27.083 --> 19:28.336
We got you!
In your face!

19:28.404 --> 19:29.558
Our boat!
Our boat!

19:29.626 --> 19:30.929
This boat!

19:33.640 --> 19:35.479
Let me go,
you fat bastard!

19:35.547 --> 19:37.453
I will never be
your sex slave!

19:37.520 --> 19:39.041
You misunderstand.

19:39.126 --> 19:41.300
I did not buy you
to be my slave.

19:41.367 --> 19:44.176
I bought you for my son,
and not to be his slave,

19:44.244 --> 19:46.417
but to be his wife.

19:46.485 --> 19:47.422
Wife?

19:47.490 --> 19:48.425
Faisal!

19:51.034 --> 19:52.472
This is Faisal,

19:52.540 --> 19:54.514
my son and the heir
to my throne.

19:55.752 --> 19:57.356
My father was correct.

19:57.423 --> 19:59.731
Your beauty
knows no bounds.

19:59.798 --> 20:01.839
Fair goddess,
it is my hope

20:01.907 --> 20:03.378
that you will agree
to be my wife,

20:03.445 --> 20:05.217
but the choice is yours.

20:05.285 --> 20:06.556
If you say "no,"

20:06.623 --> 20:08.128
I will have you flown back
to your family

20:08.195 --> 20:09.600
on our private jet.

20:09.668 --> 20:11.104
But if you say "yes,"

20:11.155 --> 20:13.079
I will spend
the rest of my days

20:13.130 --> 20:15.504
making your every wish
come true.

20:15.589 --> 20:18.850
Will you be my wife,
Princess Meg?

20:18.917 --> 20:20.889
Oh, yes! Yes!

20:25.725 --> 20:27.346
Nooooo!

20:27.430 --> 20:28.817
Stewie?

20:28.885 --> 20:31.678
Hi, Meg.

20:36.152 --> 20:38.835
Oh honey, we are so glad
to have you back

20:39.011 --> 20:40.836
but you really don't
remember anything?

20:41.092 --> 20:42.294
Not really, Mom.

20:42.363 --> 20:44.235
I mean, one minute,
I was being proposed to

20:44.303 --> 20:45.975
by a handsome
Arabian prince,

20:46.042 --> 20:47.179
and the next thing
I know,

20:47.246 --> 20:49.086
I'm waking up
in a French hospital.

20:49.153 --> 20:50.826
Oh, and we heard
from Ruth's parents.

20:50.893 --> 20:52.565
She had her tongue ripped out.

20:52.633 --> 20:53.568
(chuckling)

20:53.636 --> 20:55.743
I guess we got off easy, huh?

20:55.810 --> 20:56.947
Well, we put
all your mail

20:57.016 --> 20:58.452
on the desk in your room,
sweetheart.

20:58.520 --> 20:59.657
Thanks, Dad.

20:59.724 --> 21:01.094
I'm kidding.
You didn't get any mail.

21:01.095 --> 22:02.095
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru